{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/MockServiceReference","doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/UIComponentsReference"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":" adapts ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCat.Purchases"},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall.PaywallPlugin"},{"text":" requires. It does one job: translate ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" (defined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":") so the plugin can drive its state. Configuration of the RevenueCat SDK itself remains the caller’s responsibility."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a step-by-step integration walkthrough, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/HowToImplementService"},{"type":"text","text":". For the entitlement-mapping rules, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/EntitlementMapping","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Library-target","text":"Library target"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Product: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".product(name: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", package: \"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\"),"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Types","type":"heading","anchor":"Types"},{"level":3,"text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywallService``","type":"heading","anchor":"docSwiduxRevenueCatPaywalldocumentationSwiduxRevenueCatPaywallRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"code":["public struct RevenueCatPaywallService: PaywallService {","    public init(","        entitlementID: String,","        permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil","    )","","    public func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","    public func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>","    public func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Value type. Holds two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" identifiers and forwards every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared"},{"type":"text","text":". Cheap to construct and pass into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywall.configure"},{"type":"text","text":" has run. For production, wrap it in SwiduxPaywall’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResilientPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" so a transient read failure at launch never gates a paid user as free."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Initializer","type":"heading","anchor":"Initializer","level":4},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public init(","    entitlementID: String,","    permanentLicenseEntitlementID: String? = nil",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"entitlementID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — RevenueCat entitlement identifier that grants pro access. Surfaces as ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntitlementSnapshot.isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when active.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"permanentLicenseEntitlementID"},{"type":"text","text":" — Optional secondary identifier for a lifetime \/ permanent entitlement. Surfaces as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot.hasPermanentLicense"},{"type":"text","text":" when active. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if the app has no separate lifetime SKU."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/RevenueCatPaywall\/configure(apiKey:appUserID:userDefaults:logLevel:entitlementVerification:purchasesAreCompletedBy:storeKitVersion:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" before constructing the service. The initializer preconditions on the SDK being configured — failing fast with a named fix instead of letting ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purchases.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trap opaquely at first use. Previews and tests should construct ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]}]},{"text":"`customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading","anchor":"customerInfo-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot","level":4},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One-shot fetch. Calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfo()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and maps the result.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throws whatever the RevenueCat SDK throws ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ErrorCode.networkError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".offlineConnectionError"},{"type":"text","text":", etc.). The plugin catches the error and dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshFailed(message)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"`customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot>`","type":"heading","level":4,"anchor":"customerInfoStream-%3E-AsyncStream%3CEntitlementSnapshot%3E"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Long-lived stream. Wraps "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared.customerInfoStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and yields a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntitlementSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":" for every change RevenueCat reports — purchase, refund, family-share update, sandbox renewal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stream finishes when the underlying RevenueCat stream finishes. The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"text":" effect normally keeps it alive for the duration of the session; cancel by cancelling the consuming ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":", which terminates the stream and tears down the bridge.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The stream buffers only the newest snapshot: each yield is a complete entitlement state, so a slow consumer sees the latest value rather than replaying stale intermediate states."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A new stream first yields the customer info RevenueCat last delivered in this process, if any. RevenueCat may not have delivered one yet — on a relaunch with a fresh cache it skips the launch fetch — and then the stream stays silent until the next change, so dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".refreshCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".observeCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" to seed the state."}]},{"text":"`restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot`","type":"heading","level":4,"anchor":"restorePurchases-async-throws-%3E-EntitlementSnapshot"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the result of a restore. Reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Purchases.shared.purchasesAreCompletedBy"},{"type":"text","text":" live and branches: observer mode ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".myApp"},{"type":"text","text":") calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"syncPurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":", the default mode calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restorePurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":". RevenueCat reserves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"syncPurchases()"},{"type":"text","text":" for apps that don’t call its purchase methods, which is what observer mode means. Throws whatever the SDK throws on error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".restorePurchases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" action wraps this call and dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on success or ","type":"text"},{"code":".refreshFailed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on error.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Entitlement mapping","anchor":"Entitlement-mapping","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","c